WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.790
Filling Spider-Man's boots isn't exactly going
to be an easy task, but luckily Marvel's got

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.830
plenty of iconic heroes waiting for their
shot at the big screen.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.860
With a little luck, any one of these characters
might just be the answer to how the MCU could

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.860
replace Spider-Man.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:13.860
Ms. Marvel

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.910
Kamala Khan, also known as Ms. Marvel, has
been "embiggening" herself all across the

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.050
Marvel Universe ever since she first appeared
in 2013's Captain Marvel #17.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.910
A Pakistani-American Muslim girl with incredibly
versatile body-warping powers, Ms. Marvel

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.369
has since proven to be one of Marvel Comics'
most popular teenage heroes.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:33.750
And Kamala has already made a big name for
herself outside of the comics.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.649
She's a playable character in both the mobile
Contest of Champions game and one of the most

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:40.960
frequently-used avatars in LEGO Marvel Super-Heroes
2.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.850
She's currently the star of her own solo title
Magnificent Ms. Marvel, and the leader of

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:45.850
the team in Champions.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.770
Marvel has also recently started a new volume
of Marvel Team-Up, with Ms. Marvel as the

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:51.770
lead.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.370
Considering the circumstances, it seems particularly
fitting that the first story arc of Marvel

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.809
Team-Up includes Kamala and Peter Parker having
to deal with a Freaky Friday-style body switch.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.699
And now that Marvel has announced that Kamala
is on her way to the MCU with her own series

00:01:03.699 --> 00:01:07.580
on Disney +, there could be no better time
for her to step up and take Peter Parker's

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.530
place as the high school-aged heart and soul
of the franchise.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.590
Moon Knight

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.710
Moon Knight doesn't exactly exude the youthful
optimism of Peter Parker in fact, in most

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.290
of his appearances, he comes off as totally
mad.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.210
The vigilante's "real" name depends on which
of his multiple personalities is dominant

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:27.500
at the time he could be mercenary Marc Spector,
wealthy playboy Steven Grant, or taxi driver

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.500
Jake Lockley.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.610
And while his level of violence doesn't quite
reach the level of Marvel's more hardcore

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.960
vigilantes such as the Punisher, he certainly
isn't as forgiving as Spider-Man either.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.610
But Moon Knight and Spider-Man do find common
ground in their home, New York City.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:43.310
And like Spidey, Moon Knight isn't usually
the kind of hero who blasts off into the stars

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:44.420
to fight aliens.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:48.140
Instead, Moon Knight sticks to the streets
although admittedly his adventures can have

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.360
a more supernatural flavor than Spidey's.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.730
"I, the moon's knight of vengeance, must carry
out your luminance will.”

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:59.250
Ah… are you seriously talking to the moon?
as in, the cow jumped over?"

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.780
Still, the two characters do have a history.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:06.480
When Marvel Comics published their 2018 Infinity
Wars line-wide event, which included the creation

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.039
of a universe in which many Marvel heroes
were fused together, Moon Knight was joined

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:12.060
with Spider-Man to create Arachknight.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.349
More recently, there's been a rumor flying
around that Marvel is looking to cast Andrew

00:02:15.349 --> 00:02:18.860
Garfield to play Moon Knight in their recently
announced Disney Plus series.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.270
What a trip, right?

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.270
Nova

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:25.109
MCU fans have been speculating about Nova's
first MCU appearance ever since the release

00:02:25.109 --> 00:02:27.379
of 2014's Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:31.469
More recently the name has sprung up after
Joe Russo joked about the hero secretly appearing

00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:33.319
in the final battle of Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:37.890
This cosmic hero is a member of the Nova Corps
which, in the comics, originates on Xandar

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:44.939
the planet the Guardians save from Ronan in
their first film.

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:50.859
"Xandarians [...] nothing at all."

00:02:50.859 --> 00:02:55.010
In the comics, the Nova Corps is kind of an
intergalactic police force, somewhat similar

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.760
to DC's Green Lantern Corps.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.959
There are a couple of viable candidates who
could take on the mantle of Nova in the MCU.

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:05.379
For example, there's Marvel's earliest Nova,
Richard Rider, or the younger Sam Alexander

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:07.959
who took the name in the 2013 Nova series.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.200
While Alexander is younger, both heroes share
a strong "Peter Parker in space" vibe.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.069
They're both very similar to Parker in their
youth, the heavy responsibilities they shoulder,

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:19.291
and the fact they're often forced to push
themselves beyond their natural limits.

00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:20.291
Ironheart

00:03:20.291 --> 00:03:23.689
In Spider-Man: Far from Home, there's a lot
of talk about whether Peter Parker can grow

00:03:23.689 --> 00:03:24.970
to be the new Iron Man.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:29.060
But in the comics, Tony Stark already has
a successor and she's pretty awesome herself.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:34.250
Riri Williams, also known as Ironheart, first
appeared in 2016's Invincible Iron Man #7,

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:38.749
and circumstances led her to fill the void
Tony Stark left when he fell into a coma during

00:03:38.749 --> 00:03:40.000
Civil War II.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.439
Certified a genius at a young age, Riri uses
her genius to build her own Iron-Man-type

00:03:44.439 --> 00:03:48.400
suit after her best friend and stepfather
are killed by drive-by shooters.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.069
But Ironheart didn't disappear when Tony Stark
returned.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:54.719
She's a member of the Champions and has her
own solo title, in which she has managed to

00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:56.920
step far beyond Iron Man's shadow.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.319
Like Parker, Riri Williams is a youthful genius
whose tragic past pushes her to be the most

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:02.319
she can be.

00:04:02.319 --> 00:04:03.319
She-Hulk

00:04:03.319 --> 00:04:06.969
In April 2019, a rumor made the rounds that
Bruce Banner's cousin She-Hulk would be getting

00:04:06.969 --> 00:04:11.209
a team-up miniseries on the Disney Plus streaming
service a rumor that was confirmed when Disney

00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:14.139
announced their She-Hulk series at D23 in
August.

00:04:14.139 --> 00:04:17.470
On the surface, She-Hulk and Spider-Man don't
have too much in common.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:21.270
Spider-Man is a street-level hero who jumps
around and sticks to walls, while She-Hulk

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.320
is a powerhouse brute who can knock down walls.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.190
Peter Parker is a high school student while
Jennifer Walters is an accomplished lawyer.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:30.600
But one thing Parker and Walters have in common
is that they're both downright hilarious.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.760
As well as that, both characters often wrestle
with how they can juggle their normal lives

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.950
with their "super lives".

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:40.000
As far as the MCU is concerned, they could
also cover similar story ground, both living

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.040
in the shadow of two older, more seasoned
heroes.

